\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Counting basis of the weight}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Order the edges of a [selected Gaussian background](fdip-005A)
and take the counting basis of edge functions. Pointwise
multiplication by #{w} is then the diagonal endomorphism
##{W=\operatorname{diag}(w).}
The same ordering of vertices makes #{m^2I} scalar. The operator
#{Q=d^*Wd+m^2I} does not depend on that order.}
